# LeakSanitizer suppressions for third-party leaks that we cannot fix in this
# project. All entries below are leaks in gstreamer/libav internals — not in
# ros_camera_server code.

# gst_init() permanently registers a default log handler whose GSList node is
# never freed; gstreamer has no de-init counterpart.
leak:gst_init

# gst_debug_add_log_function leaks one GSList node per registered handler:
# the implementation copies the list, prepends, then swaps the pointer; the
# original head node is not freed. We do call gst_debug_remove_log_function_by_data
# in ~CameraServer to release the LogFuncEntry, but the list-node leak is in
# gstreamer itself.
leak:gst_debug_add_log_function

# h264parse / libgstvideoparsersbad allocates av_malloc-backed scratch buffers
# in gst_pad_push paths that are not always reaped when the pipeline is taken
# to NULL during shutdown.
leak:libavutil
leak:libgstvideo
